carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:1:"""ASD module — drift correction for closed-loop self-updating identity memories.
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:4:  a memory-agnostic wrapper around ANY identity memory that (i) picks a candidate, (ii) reports a confidence on any
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:5:  scale, (iii) exposes an update hook. Per decision tick it keeps a tempered, confidence-weighted evidence count per
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:6:  persistent tracklet  L_k <- lam*L_k + (0.5 + rank(conf))*1[k = memory pick]  and, when argmax_k L_k disagrees with
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:8:  Rationale (acot_note/1001_innovation-design.md): self-update makes the memory's errors autocorrelated, so evidence
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:10:ABLATIONS: filter_kind="resid" (equal weights), "bayes" (untempered sticky HMM), gate_memory=False (commit-only).
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:11:LEGACY (negative results, kept for reproducibility): modes "rule"/"learned" = frozen appearance+language anchor with
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:25:                 tau: float = 0.1, kappa: float = 0.25, h: float = 2.0, refractory: int = 3,
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:28:                 gate_memory: bool = True, filter_kind: str = "bayes", resid_decay: float = 0.98,
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:33:        self.tau, self.kappa, self.h, self.refractory = float(tau), float(kappa), float(h), int(refractory)
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:44:        # 'spec' = sequential SPEC identification: integrate language evidence per actor over the window, anchor
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:45:        # to the argmax actor's crops and correct M if it disagrees (also fixes wrong cold-start locks).
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:48:        # filter mode (ASD-IF): sticky Bayes filter over persistent tracklets; the memory's pick is a noisy
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:49:        # observation whose error rate q is set by the rank of its confidence within a sliding window
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:50:        # (scale-free → memory-agnostic, no per-memory calibration). Output = MAP tracklet (posterior gating).
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:52:        self.gate_memory = bool(gate_memory)          # ablation: False = override commitment only, memory still self-updates
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:53:        assert filter_kind in ("bayes", "resid", "tempered"), filter_kind
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:54:        self.filter_kind, self.resid_decay = filter_kind, float(resid_decay)   # 'resid' = longest-residence heuristic
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:58:        # 1004 deployable v2 · ABSENCE HYPOTHESIS: the posterior also ranges over tracklets NOT visible this tick (seen
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:59:        # within the last `absent_max` ticks). If its MAP tracklet is currently unseen (occluded / out of frame), PGIF
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:61:        # pick the best VISIBLE tracklet — the forced choice is what turns a target occlusion into a wrong lock.
carla_uav_tracking/rollout/asd.py:62:        # The evidence update itself is unchanged.
